Add MIR_ROTR: a 64-bit rotate-right instruction.

Lambda's inline double-boxing path (transpile-mir.cpp emit_box_double and the
LambdaJS twin in js_mir_calls_boxing_types.cpp) needs a rotate to move the
double's sign bit into the tag position without a call.  Both emit
`ROTR bits, 63` -- rotate left by one expressed as rotate right by 63 -- so the
constant-count form is the hot one; the dynamic-count form is provided for
completeness.

Rotate-LEFT is deliberately absent: aarch64 has no rotate-left, and every
rotate-left by n is a rotate-right by 64-n, so a single right-rotate opcode
covers both directions without a per-target lowering.

  mir.h             new INSN_EL (ROTR) opcode, placed after the shift group
  mir.c             matching insn_descs entry ("rotr", 3 int operands)
  mir-interp.c      ROTR64 macro + dispatch label + SCASE.  The count is masked
                    to 0..63 so a zero count is well defined (a bare
                    `p1 << (64 - p2)` would be UB at p2 == 0)
  mir-gen-x86_64.c  ror r,cl (D3 /1) and ror r,imm8 (C1 /1); target_machinize
                    only forces the count into cl for a dynamic count, so a
                    constant keeps its imm8 form
  mir-gen-aarch64.c rorv Rd,Rn,Rm for a dynamic count and extr Rd,Rn,Rn,#imms
                    (the ror alias) for a constant one, via a new 'SO' operand
                    kind holding a 0..63 constant rotate count

Applies to upstream vnmakarov/mir at 99c65079038f3ba9242ef646f308c266cfd7a8e5.

